# Liaison IDE hop — leftover goal release

**Invariant:** `liaison_ide_hop.ok ∧ departing_attended_tab ∧ native_goal_active ⇒ UpdateGoal(complete)`
same turn — **before** the `RETIRED → <transcript_id>` line. Skip `CreateGoal` on pickup. Harness
`retire_departing_tab` cannot call UpdateGoal (Cursor-native).

| Meaning | `UpdateGoal(complete)` on hop? |
|---|---|
| House arc / scoreboard fully closed | Yes (arc close) |
| Hop landed; leftover native goal still injecting | **Yes** (stop continuation-wake; 11912) |
| Hop landed; no native goal | No-op — watchers + `--heartbeat 1200` are the wakes |
| Loop stopped; no hop | Only if a leftover goal is injecting or the objective is met |

**Tool (verbatim, only if a goal is active):** `CallDynamicTool(namespace="cursor", toolName="UpdateGoal", arguments={"status":"complete"})`.

**Script cues:** `liaison-ide-hop.py` JSON field `goal_release`; stderr `LIAISON_HOP_TAB_GOAL_RELEASE` (see
`libs/bus_watch/ide_hop_retire.GOAL_RELEASE`).

**Successor:** rebuild each ARM label (`watch-supervise.sh stop --label L`; `start --label L --`
from `tmp/watchers/<L>.argv.json`; then `tail --label L`) + `liaison-tick.py --loop --heartbeat 1200`
(20 min backup to re-arm / check watcher health). Do not `CreateGoal`. Departing tab tore the
pollers down — a tail-only ARM would attach to a dead pid.

**Anti-pattern:** Minting `CreateGoal` so the Goals panel is non-empty — Cursor then injects unthrottled
continuation wakes. Primary house wake is watcher `notify_on_output`.

Playbook: Use the `liaison` skill § Wakes · command `.cursor/commands/liaison.md` Hop section.
